  "context_identity": "profile/experiment/target core/physical family/country/window/scope; use profile-selected Solsoe key when enumerating Denmark country targets. Enumerate every declared window regardless of target observation availability. No pooling or joint quantitative ancestry of SOLSOE81/83 in one profile.",
  "exclusion_policy": "Build the structural allowed training set from the six profile places after whole native physical-family and, for country folds, whole target-country exclusion. Swedish-only additionally excludes every non-SE source. Every excluded source receives its exact reason. Native source-country labels define declared grouping, not qualified geographic decisions or coordinate corrections.",
  "required_training_policy": "Every structurally allowed place must have a supported positive same-window source panel. If any required source window is empty/refused/zero/invalid, retain all required owners and refuse BOTH prediction methods for that context. No dropping, renormalizing over available sources, window substitution, zero imputation or fallback. Other contexts continue. Fixed complete cohorts make changes in training support explicit.",
  "weight_policy": "After structural exclusions, equal-place assigns1/n places. Equal-country assigns1/C allowed countries and then1/n_country within each. Construct weights before source availability/refusal; never from full/global country totals or target counts. Both methods use the identical required places and weights.",
